;    1: TDecorate(count=20, unk2=16755455, unk3=4294967295, unk4=0, unk5=1, unk6=0, unk7=4294967295, unk8=, ruby=, unk10=4294967295, unk11=4294967295)
;    2: TDecorate(count=2, unk2=65535, unk3=4294967295, unk4=0, unk5=1, unk6=0, unk7=4294967295, unk8=, ruby=, unk10=4294967295, unk11=4294967295)
; Display conditions:
;    0: TWdCondition(count=770, target=)
; Links:
;    0: TWdLink(count=702, event=, unk3=)
;---------------------------------------
; BEGIN DECOMPILED SCRIPT
;---------------------------------------
<SCENARIO VER="105">
{PLAYSND "SE\pc_keyboard.ogg" "SE" "REPEAT" "1000" "0"}
{CREATECG "000" "グラフィック\背景\五島パソコン.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "C" "T" "0" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
{CREATECG "文字カウント画像" "グラフィック\システム\文字カウント画像.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "C" "B" "0" "1" "0" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
<TXSPN>I'm going to get <STYLE ID="1">Kogori-senpai</STYLE> onto the starting lineup no matter what, no matter what!
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
I absolutely want <STYLE ID="1">Kogori-senpai</STYLE> to shine!
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
What I can do is put together effective training menus like this and have her carry them out.<PG>
No matter how good the menu is, it's no use unless I keep <STYLE ID="1">Kogori-senpai</STYLE>'s motivation up.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
I'll build the menu so she gets even a little sense of achievement, so her drive lasts even a little longer.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
And I'll carefully work out a strategy for how I should deal with <STYLE ID="1">Kogori-senpai</STYLE>, too.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
I'm fighting too!<PG>
{STOPSND "SE" "500" "PASS"}
That said...
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Time-wise, it's pretty tough...
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
It's not just <STYLE ID="1">Kogori-senpai</STYLE>; everyone else is getting better too.<PG>
Yeah, I'm only looking it up out of curiosity.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Out of curiosity...
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Let's see... 
{PAUSE ""}
Search for doping―<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{PLAYSND "SE\duble_clicks.ogg" "VOICE" "NORMAL" "1000" "0"}
{CHANGECG "000" "グラフィック\背景\検索.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "1000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
Hmm, so there are all kinds of doping drugs.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Anabolic steroids, sibutramine―
{PAUSE ""}
and ephedrine.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Ephedrine, if I remember right, is a precursor of methamphetamine, a stimulant drug, and it's in cold medicine too.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
It stimulates the sympathetic nervous system, so supposedly you can perform beyond your usual level.<PG>
But still... no matter how much ephedrine you use, the effect is limited, and I can't exactly make her take a ton of cold medicine.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
If I remember right, the strength you only find in an emergency happens when the sympathetic nerves get overexcited and the limiter on the muscles comes off, right?
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
If only there were some way to trigger the strength you only find in an emergency on purpose.<PG>
The ideal drug, one that triggers the strength you only find in an emergency...
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Does anything like that exist in this world?
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Well, if something like that existed, it would probably throw the balance of the world off, though.<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "000" "グラフィック\背景\五島パソコン.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "1000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
Anyway, more importantly, I have to put together the training menu!
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
The <STYLE ID="2">Goto</STYLE> Menu has got to be way, way more effective than ephedrine!
{WAIT "100" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{DELETECG "文字カウント画像" "1" "0" "0" "0" "" "0"}
<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{PLAYSND "SE\pc_keyboard.ogg" "SE" "REPEAT" "1000" "0"}
{STOPSND "SE" "3000" "PASS"}
{DELETECG "000" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0"}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
<PG>
{}
<EVENT VALUE="MESEND">
;---------------------------------------
; END DECOMPILED SCRIPT
;---------------------------------------